# Roblox Luau Game Architecture & Workflow Instructions

Build and maintain this Roblox game completely in code (`.luau` files) using the **Rojo + Rokit** external workflow so the entire game—maps, 3D models, UI, sound wiring, AI bots, and server/client logic—lives in Git and can be imported into Roblox Studio via three `.rbxm` files (`Shared.rbxm`, `Server.rbxm`, `Client.rbxm`) or a full `.rbxlx` place file.

---

## 1. CLI Toolchain (`rokit.toml`)
Use **Rokit** (`~/.rokit/bin`) to manage and run all CLI tools from the terminal:
```toml
[tools]
rojo = "rojo-rbx/rojo@7.7.1"
selene = "Kampfkarren/selene@0.32.0"
stylua = "JohnnyMorganz/StyLua@2.6.0"
luau-lsp = "JohnnyMorganz/luau-lsp@1.70.1"
luau = "luau-lang/luau@0.746"
lune = "lune-org/lune@0.11.1"
```
- **`.luaurc`:** `{ "languageMode": "strict" }` — every `.luau` file must begin with `--!strict`.
- **`selene.toml`:** `std = "roblox"` (`0 errors, 0 warnings` required).
- **`stylua.toml`:** `column_width = 120`, `indent_type = "Tabs"`, `indent_width = 4`, `quote_style = "AutoPreferDouble"`.

